{
  "_comment": [
    "The one inventory of test gates, read by scripts/test.py (the full gate) and",
    "scripts/test-affected.py (the gates a change touches). A gate is a suite script",
    "under tests/ or scripts/, or a builtin set of per-file checks ('syntax': every",
    "tests/syntax file through check --syntax-only; 'goldens': every tests/runtime and",
    "tests/visitor .spr with a .out golden, plus the exhaustiveness, explain and JSON",
    "envelope checks). Gates run in the listed order in the final record. A gate with",
    "'serial' names why it cannot share the machine with other gates; the serial group",
    "runs alone, one gate at a time, after the parallel group. 'full': false marks a gate",
    "that scripts/verify.py runs on its own and test.py leaves out; test-affected.py",
    "still selects it."
  ],
